From: SORABBYNGO Engineering <kernel@sorabbyngo.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0012] audit: sorabbyngo SHA-256 chained kernel audit log

Extends the Linux audit subsystem with a Sorabbyngo-specific SHA-256
chained audit log. Every security-relevant kernel event is written to
an append-only, hash-chained log that mirrors the userspace CML audit
ledger.

The chain works as follows:
  entry[n].hash = SHA256(entry[n-1].hash || timestamp || pid || op || detail)

This means tampering with any entry breaks all subsequent hashes,
making the log forensically sound for Kenya DPA 2019 compliance and
IEC 62443 audit requirements.

Events captured at kernel level:
  - All Sorabbyngo LSM denials
  - eBPF program loads (success and failure)
  - NodeID reads from /proc/sorabbyngo/nodeid
  - Byngonet peer additions/removals
  - Pledge/unveil calls
  - W^X violations
  - Module loads/unloads (all, not just Sorabbyngo)
  - Privilege escalations (setuid, capability changes)

The chain root hash is exposed at /proc/sorabbyngo/audit_root.
Userspace sorabbyngo-security verify_chain.py reads this to confirm
kernel and userspace audit logs are consistent.

Ring buffer size: 4096 entries (configurable via Kconfig).
Overflow policy: oldest entry dropped, gap recorded in next entry.
